{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33/events","html_url":"https://github.com/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33","id":6133425770,"node_id":"I_kwDORt12rc8AAAABbZSmag","number":33,"title":"mcp-server-review: add tool definition integrity check (rug pull detection)","user":{"login":"Dee-Tee11","id":216906516,"node_id":"U_kgDODO27FA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216906516?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11","html_url":"https://github.com/Dee-Tee11","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dee-Tee11/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-10-31T09:40:44Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T19:42:56Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\nThe `mcp-server-review` skill and play don't currently check for **rug pull** attacks: an MCP server changing its tool definitions (description, schema or annotations) *after* the user has reviewed and approved them.\n\nThe closest existing step is **6. Supply Chain** (\"assess update mechanism\"), but that covers package updates. It does not cover server-side changes to tool definitions, which are especially relevant for remote MCP servers, where there is no package update to review at all. A one-time approval is currently treated as permanent.\n\nThis is not theoretical: CVE-2025-54136 (\"MCPoison\") was a rug-pull flaw in Cursor, which did not re-check MCP configurations after the first approval until v1.3 (July 2025).\n\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\nAdd a new step to both `skills/mcp-server-review/SKILL.md` and `plays/mcp-server-review.md`, e.g. **Tool Definition Integrity (Rug Pull)**, that verifies whether the MCP client/agent:\n\n1. **Pins** each approved tool by hashing its *complete* definition (name, description, `inputSchema`, `outputSchema` and annotations), not only the description. A flipped `readOnlyHint` or `destructiveHint` can change approval behavior without any visible description change.\n2. **Detects drift** by comparing the current definition against the pinned hash at least once per session (ideally before each call), including handling of `notifications/tools/list_changed`.\n3. On any change, **blocks** the tool, **shows the user a human-readable diff** of what changed, and **requires re-approval** before the tool can be used again.\n\nEach missing control would be reported as a finding using `templates/finding.md`.\n\nI'd also suggest adding MCP-specific references to the skill's OWASP References, which currently only list LLM Top 10 and Web Top 10 items:\n- OWASP MCP Top 10 – MCP03: Tool Poisoning (which covers rug pulls)\n- OWASP MCP Security Cheat Sheet (Tool Description & Schema Integrity), which already recommends pinning tool definitions with cryptographic hashes and re-prompting for consent when they change\n\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\n- Folding this into step 6 (Supply Chain). I think a separate step is clearer, since rug pulls happen at runtime and are independent of the package update mechanism.\n- Covering it in `agent-security-audit` instead. That play focuses on agent permissions and guardrails; tool definition integrity is specific to MCP, so `mcp-server-review` seems the better fit. A cross-reference could be added there.\n\n**Additional context**\nThis isn't just a theoretical concern for me: I've dealt with this problem in practice and implemented this kind of control (tool definition pinning, drift detection and re-approval with a diff) at my workplace. I'd be glad to bring that experience into the play.\n\nI'm happy to submit a PR for this (SKILL.md + play + references). Before starting, I'd like to confirm the approach fits the project's direction.\n\nIf you'd like to discuss this further, feel free to reach out to me here https://www.linkedin.com/in/diogo-teixeira-9b108423b/ or by email diogoluisteixeira@gmail.com.\n\ncc @cmaenner ","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OWASP/secure-agent-playbook/issues/33/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}